    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1095">

                <pb facs="0798" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg682"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/4090.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Brazilian Minister at Mexico City.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>We are much pleased to learn of your successful efforts to secure train for
                    Americans desiring to leave Mexico; also gratified to know that General Huerta
                    has given assurance of protection so far as his forces are concerned to
                    foreigners returning to Tampico District for the care of the oil wells. General
                    Carranza has also promised protection where he is in control.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
